, Agent 2 now also supports C. We can reinforce that C's strengths (anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership) outweigh his criticism and organization issues, and that the interpersonal concerns of B and D are more severe.\n\nWe can also note that we still lack evidence on C's teamwork and stress resilience, but given the current evidence, C remains best.\n\nThus produce public message: I agree with Agent 2, maintain vote for C, explain why.\n\nMake sure to include explicit facts: \"can anticipate dangerous situations\", \"sees complex connections\", \"excellent spatial vision\", \"very good leadership qualities\", \"sometimes not good at taking criticism\", \"can be unorganized\". Also mention B's \"makes nasty remarks\", D's \"regarded as arrogant\". Emphasize crew cooperation risk.\n\nNow produce output sections."}
